# Sold Page Walkthrough
Sold page is pretty straightforward so I will make this a one page guide only. Plus I'm pretty tired of explaining this stuff. I already make the application very user friendly so me making this docs just second guessing my audience right. Lol, you cannot underestimate someone's stupidity I guess

## Sold Page Anatomy

### Per Month Section
This is separated by per month section. This is collapsible but expanded by default. You can see the timeline of each transactions made 

### Transaction Card
Every sold items are part of a transaction. Transaction is the done deal made by a seller and a customer. A transaction can consist of 1 or more sold items, that's why is encapsulated by a transaction.
In the card. It consist of the thumbnail, transaction sold date. Total amount sold, the channel and how many items were sold

## Transaction Details
### Expanded Info
This just show similar to transdaction card but with expanded information. It shows also if the transaction was a bundled transaction or per piece. If you didn't know the difference, please reed the selling items page first. Don't make a fool out of yourself

### Action Button
Action button is just the back button and undo button. Now this is the undo button the item details page is referring to. This does undo not just one sold items but the whole transaction itself. The app doesn't have an edit transaction but it does have an undo button. If you think the app should have an edit button, just state your concern here lol.




